title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tiddlers/sigil-helu
tags: $:/tags/Global lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/SharktoothSigil
lar-kind: pragma
lar-pono-uri: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/helu
lar-see-also: \function
lar-open-pattern: <<~\s*helu\s+([\w-]+)(?:\s+([^>]*?))?\s*>>
lar-close-pattern: <<~\/helu\s*>>
lar-example: <<~ helu tally "[tag[x]count[]]">>
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<!-- helu — a NAMED FILTER FUNCTION and the filter it reckons. THE NAME FIRST, THE FILTER SECOND:

         <<~ helu tally "[tag[x]count[]]">>

     //helu// counts, enumerates, reckons. Where `wehe` declares a body that RENDERS, helu declares
     one that COMPUTES — the body yields a filter result set, never wikitext.

     THE PAGE STAYS CLEAR. Its law reads "register a function definition only, producing no render
     output", so the definition hands the compile layer a data annotation and leaves the reader
     nothing to step over.

     THE FILTER RIDES QUOTED. It carries brackets, colons and prose; unquoted, every `word:` binds a
     parameter nobody named and the slot receives nothing. -->

\procedure ~helu(p1:"" p2:"")
<span class="lar-helu" data-helu-name=<<p1>> data-helu-filter=<<p2>> hidden="true"/>
\end
